<p>
  <%= trust.name %> respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal
  data we collect, why, and how we protect it, in line with the Digital
  Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the Information Technology Act, 2000.
</p>

<h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account:</strong> name, email, mobile number and a hashed password (we never store your actual password).</li>
  <li><strong>Donations:</strong> name, email, mobile number, amount, cause, purpose, and if you give them: address, PAN, dedication ("in memory of"), preferred seva date, gotra (for temple donations) and a message. We also keep the payment mode and transaction ID.</li>
  <li><strong>Membership:</strong> name, email, mobile number, amount and transaction ID.</li>
  <li><strong>Medical help requests:</strong> patient's name, Aadhaar number, date of birth, mobile number, email, illness, hospital and the name of the person who referred them.</li>
  <li><strong>Volunteers:</strong> name, mobile number, email, city, areas of interest and availability.</li>
  <li><strong>Event registrations and messages:</strong> name, mobile number, email, number of people and your message.</li>
  <li><strong>People we help</strong> (Anand Dham residents, Kanyadaan families, children in Vidya and Poshan): the details needed to check need and give help, collected in person and kept in the Trust's records.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical:</strong> a session cookie that keeps you logged in, a language cookie, and basic server logs (such as IP address) for security.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not collect card numbers, UPI PINs or bank passwords. These are handled
  directly by our payment gateway, PayU.
</p>

<h2>2. Why we use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To process donations and memberships and send receipts and certificates.</li>
  <li>To use your donation for the cause, purpose and seva date you chose, and to print your dedication on the receipt.</li>
  <li>To prepare donor statements the law asks of a charitable trust (such as Form 10BD, which needs PAN and address), once the Trust is registered for it.</li>
  <li>To check and respond to requests for help.</li>
  <li>To contact volunteers about drives and events, and to manage event registrations.</li>
  <li>To send monthly reminders, only if you chose monthly giving.</li>
  <li>To run your account, keep the Trust's accounts and prevent fraud.</li>
</ul>
<p>We use your data only with your consent, which you give by ticking the consent box on our forms, or where the law requires us to keep it.</p>

<h2>3. Children and elders</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Data about children in our programmes is collected from their parent or guardian and used only for their education and nutrition support.</li>
  <li>We do not publish names, addresses or Aadhaar numbers of children, elders or families we help.</li>
  <li>Photos of beneficiaries are published only with their consent (or a guardian's, for children).</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. How we protect it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Stored records are encrypted (AES-256-GCM) and backed up regularly.</li>
  <li>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt.</li>
  <li>Only the last 4 digits of an Aadhaar number are printed on receipts.</li>
  <li>Only the trustees can open the admin area, which is protected by a password.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>PayU</strong>, to process payments.</li>
  <li><strong>Our email provider (Google Gmail)</strong>, to send receipts and replies.</li>
  <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong>, only if you choose to message us there.</li>
  <li>Hospitals, only to confirm a medical help request you sent.</li>
  <li>The Income Tax Department and other authorities, only when the law requires it.</li>
</ul>
<p>We never sell, rent or publish your personal data.</p>

<h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
<p>
  Donation and payment records are kept for at least 8 years, as required for
  a charitable trust's accounts and audits. Volunteer, event and message
  records are kept for as long as they are useful for that purpose, and then deleted.
</p>

<h2>7. Your rights</h2>
<p>
  You can ask us to see, correct or delete your personal data, or withdraw
  your consent, by contacting us below. Records we must keep by law (such as
  donation records) cannot be deleted before the legal period ends.
</p>

<h2>8. Cookies</h2>
<p>
  We use one cookie to keep you logged in and one to remember your language.
  We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.
</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>
<p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

